# Every text file is LF in the repository and LF on disk, on every OS.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for
# Windows default) writes CRLF, and that reaches two things that read
# source files as bytes: the markdown that app/src-tauri include_str!s
# and ships as the skills and agent files gavin writes into a user's
# repo, and the app tests that grep component source. A release built
# on Windows must not carry different bytes from one built on a mac.
#
# A checkout made before this file existed keeps CRLF on disk until
# its files are re-checked out; see CLAUDE.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-exact, never converted.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.raw binary
